==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:produccioun<ety:bor<fro:production<ety:der<la:prōductiō>>>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|produccioun}}, from {{der|en|fro|production}}, from {{der|en|la|productio|prōductiō, prōductiōnem|a lengthening, prolonging}}. Equivalent to {{suf|en|produce|tion}}. See {{m|en|produce}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɹəˈdʌkʃən/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɹəˈdʌkʃn̩/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-production.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-production.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{hyph|en|pro|duc|tion}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|creating}} The act of [[produce|producing]], [[making]] or [[creating]] something. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|The widget making machine is being used for '''production''' now.}}
# {{senseid|en|showing}} The act of bringing something forward, out, etc., for use or consideration. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Saki Reginald in Russia|story=The Lost Sanjak|pages=16–17|pageref=17|passage=I tramped to a neighbouring market-town, and, late as the hour was, the '''production''' of a few shillings procured me supper and a night's lodging in a cheap coffee-house.}}
# {{senseid|en|passive}} The act of being [[produce]]d.
#: {{ux|en|The widgets are coming out of '''production''' now.}}
# {{senseid|en|amount}} The total amount [[produce]]d.
#: {{ux|en|They hope to increase spaghetti '''production''' next year.}}
#* {{RQ:Browne Hydriotaphia|chapter=III|page=136|passage=The exiguity and ſmallneſſe of ſome ſeeds extending to large '''productions''' is one of the magnalities of nature, ſomewhat illuſtrating the work of the Creation, and vaſt '''production''' from nothing.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jon Gambrell|title=United Arab Emirates will leave OPEC in a blow to the oil cartel|magazine=w:AP News|url=https://apnews.com/article/opec-united-arab-emirates-leaving-cartel-4966108c3fafacb67181152216deda14|date=2026-04-28|passage=The UAE’s decision had been rumored as a possibility for some time, as it pushed back in recent years against OPEC '''production''' quotas it felt had been too low — meaning it wasn’t able to sell as much oil to the world as it had wanted.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260429193339/https://apnews.com/article/opec-united-arab-emirates-leaving-cartel-4966108c3fafacb67181152216deda14}}
# {{senseid|en|theater}} The presentation of a theatrical work.
#: {{ux|en|If you get the chance, try and catch the new '''production''' of "Hamlet."}}
# {{senseid|en|complicating}} An [[occasion]] or [[activity]] made more [[complicated]] than [[necessary]].
#: {{ux|en|He made a simple meal into a huge '''production'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|product}} That which is [[manufacture]]d or is ready for manufacturing in volume (as opposed to a [[prototype]] or [[conceptual]] [[model]]).
#: {{ux|en|This is the final '''production''' model.}}
# {{senseid|en|prolonging}} The act of [[lengthen]]ing out or [[prolong]]ing. <!--Webster 1913-->
# {{senseid|en|zoology}} {{lb|en|zoology}} An [[extension]] or [[protrusion]]. <!--Chambers 1908-->
# {{senseid|en|computing}} {{lb|en|computing}} A [[rewrite rule]] specifying a symbol substitution that can be recursively performed to generate new symbol sequences. (More information on [[w:Production (computer science)|Wikipedia]].)
#: {{ux|en|Each '''production''' is implemented with a function.}}
# {{senseid|en|programming}} {{lb|en|programming|uncountable}} The [[environment]] where finished code runs, as opposed to [[staging]] or [[development]].
#: {{co|en|'''production''' environment}}
#: {{co|en|live '''production''' database}}
# {{senseid|en|legal}} {{lb|en|Scots law|in the plural}} Written documents produced in support of the action or defence.
# {{senseid|en|linguistics}} {{lb|en|linguistics}} Writing viewed as the process of producing a text in any medium (written, spoken, signed, multimodal, nonverbal), consisting of several steps such as conceptualization, formulation, expression and revision.

